biomarker_reliability_and_future_focus.reliability_assessment:
Lactic acid levels were reliably measured using a Biosen C-Line blood analysis system (coefficient of variation 
 1.5%, detection range 0.5-40 mmol/L). Creatine kinase levels were measured using a Fuji Dri-Chem 4000i (detection range 10-2000 U/L). Heart rate was monitored with Polar HR devices, and HRmax was estimated using 220-age. However, Creatine Kinase (CK) is considered an indirect and highly variable marker, influenced by training status, fiber type, genetics, and exercise modality, so its findings should be interpreted with caution. Statistical power (1 - 
) reached 0.8, indicating a reasonable sample size.
